@startuml f4-event-router-dispatch
title F4 — Event Router dispatches a queued task (REST to executor)

|ER|
start
:Query ER DB
 (next pending task for the
  next available executor);

|ER|
:Open ER DB read;
:SELECT task
 -> task_spec
 + scope_token
 + routing_target;
:Close ER DB read;

|ER|
:UPDATE task SET status=preparing;

|ER|
:REST POST /dispatch
 to Executor X
 { task_spec + scope_token };

|EX (executor X)|
:Receive REST POST /dispatch;
:Pull pre-built agent image (OCI);
:Prepare container runtime;

|AG|
:Container about to start;
:Read secrets via open env (see F5);
:Start agent loop (see F6);

stop

note right
  No queues. ER queries its own DB,
  pushes the task to the executor
  via REST.
  Executor receives full
  task_spec + scope_token
  in the REST payload.
  GW is not on this path.
end note

@enduml